############## Circuit Breaker #####################
1. Add a resilience library dependency in your pom.xml (use resilience4j\-spring\-boot3 for Spring Boot3).
2. Enable the circuit breaker module in your configuration ( application.yml or application.properties ).

3. Define a circuit breaker instance with thresholds (failure %, slow call limits, wait duration).
4. Wrap the external API call in your service with the circuit breaker annotation or programmatic API.
5. Provide a fallback method that returns a safe response when the breaker is open.
6. Record only relevant exceptions as failures (e.g.5xx, timeouts) and ignore expected ones (e.g.4xx).
7. Add metrics or logs to observe breaker state changes.
8. Write tests to simulate failures and verify open\ / half-open\ / closed transitions.





